{
 "duration": 50.238,
 "language": "pt",
 "text": "What if you fell into a black hole? If it's a small one, you'd never even make it inside. Gravity pulls your feet so much harder than your head, you'd be stretched like a noodle. Scientists really call it spaghettification. So let's pick a giant one. Like the black hole in the center of our galaxy. Four million times heavier than the Sun. You cross the edge, the event horizon, and you feel... nothing. No wall. No bump. But your friend, watching from far away, sees something creepy. You slow down, turn red, and freeze at the edge. Forever. Inside, every direction points to the center. Nothing gets out. Not even light. From there, you'd have about one minute left. And what's at the very center? Nobody knows. Not even the smartest scientists alive. So, would you jump in, just to find out?",
